      <section class="section" id="research">
        <h3>Featured Research</h3>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Selected peer-reviewed work on endoscopic spine surgery, adult spinal deformity,
          and machine learning–based risk prediction.
        </p>

        <h4>Endoscopic Spine Surgery</h4>
        <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
          <div class="card">
            <div class="card-title">
              Percutaneous Endoscopic Thoracic Discectomy in the Upper and Midthoracic
              Spine: A Technical Note
            </div>
            <div class="card-meta">Neurospine, 2019</div>
            <p class="card-text">
              Technical description and clinical outcomes of percutaneous transforaminal
              endoscopic thoracic discectomy in the upper and midthoracic spine, expanding
              the indications of full endoscopic surgery beyond the lumbar region.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <div class="card-title">
              Transforaminal Endoscopic Thoracic Discectomy with Foraminoplasty for the
              Treatment of Thoracic Disc Herniation
            </div>
            <div class="card-meta">Journal of Spine Surgery, 2020</div>
            <p class="card-text">
              Describes transforaminal endoscopic thoracic discectomy (TETD) with
              foraminoplasty for symptomatic thoracic disc herniation, focusing on safe
              access, decompression, and complication avoidance.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <div class="card-title">
              Percutaneous Transforaminal Endoscopic Lumbar Interbody Fusion: Clinical and
              Radiological Results of Mean 46-Month Follow-Up
